[ 2026-10-05 04:34:59,466 ] groq._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/openai/v1/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-f8854dc3-041f-42d7-84a7-c2a4b1971d6e', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': "Use this extracted information to call the tool directly:\n- Problem Type: mechanics\n- Operation: ['acceleration']\n- Parameters: {'mass_A': 20.0, 'mass_B': 10.0, 'mass_pulley': 6.0, 'radius_pulley': 0.2, 'coefficient_friction': 0.25, 'applied_force': 35.0, 'gravity': 9.81}\nDo not ask for missing info, just call the appropriate tool."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "A 20 kg block A rests on a rough horizontal table and is connected by a massless, inextensible cable to a 10 kg block B hanging vertically over a solid disk pulley. The pulley has a mass of 6 kg and a radius of 0.20 m, and its moment of inertia about its axle is I = (1/2)MR². The coefficient of kinetic friction between block A and the table is 0.25. A constant horizontal force of 35 N is applied to block A in the direction away from the pulley. The cable does not slip on the pulley, and the pulley axle is frictionless. Take g = 9.81 m/s². Starting from rest, determine the direction of motion of the system, the linear acceleration of blocks A and B, the angular acceleration of the pulley, the tension in the cable on the A side, the tension in the cable on the B side, and the kinetic friction force on block A. Show the governing equations, clearly identify the forces and torques, and verify the final results using Newton's second law and the rotational equation for the pulley."}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_force', 'description': "Calculate force using Newton's second law.\n\nFormula:\n    F = m * a\n\nArgs:\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Force in Newtons (N).", 'parameters': {'properties': {'mass': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['mass', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_mass', 'description': 'Calculate mass from force and acceleration.\n\nFormula:\n    m = F / a\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Mass in kilograms (kg).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_acceleration', 'description': 'Calculate acceleration from force and mass.\n\nFormula:\n    a = F / m\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n\nReturns:\n    Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'mass': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'mass'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_torque', 'description': 'Calculate torque.\n\nFormula:\n    τ = r * F * sin(θ)\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    lever_arm: Distance from pivot in meters (m).\n    angle: Angle between force and lever arm in degrees.\n\nReturns:\n    Torque in Newton-meters (N·m).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'lever_arm': {'type': 'number'}, 'angle': {'default': 90.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'lever_arm'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_work', 'description': 'Calculate mechanical work.\n\nFormula:\n    W = F * d * cos(θ)\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    displacement: Displacement in meters (m).\n    angle: Angle between force and displacement in degrees.\n\nReturns:\n    Work in Joules (J).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'displacement': {'type': 'number'}, 'angle': {'default': 0.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'displacement'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_energy', 'description': 'Calculate kinetic energy.\n\nFormula:\n    KE = 1/2 * m * v²\n\nArgs:\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n    velocity: Velocity in meters per second (m/s).\n\nReturns:\n    Kinetic energy in Joules (J).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'mass': {'type': 'number'}, 'velocity': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['mass', 'velocity'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_power', 'description': 'Calculate mechanical power.\n\nFormula:\n    P = W / t\n\nArgs:\n    work: Work in Joules (J).\n    time: Time in seconds (s).\n\nReturns:\n    Power in Watts (W).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'work': {'type': 'number'}, 'time': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['work', 'time'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_stress', 'description': 'Calculate normal stress.\n\nFormula:\n    σ = F / A\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    area: Cross-sectional area in square meters (m²).\n\nReturns:\n    Stress in Pascals (Pa).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'area': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'area'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_strain', 'description': 'Calculate normal strain.\n\nFormula:\n    ε = ΔL / L₀\n\nArgs:\n    change_in_length: Change in length in meters (m).\n    original_length: Original length in meters (m).\n\nReturns:\n    Strain (dimensionless).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'change_in_length': {'type': 'number'}, 'original_length': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['change_in_length', 'original_length'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'convert_force